description:
Design a circuit that acts as an 8-to-3 encoder. This module takes an 8-bit wide input, `A`, and produces a 3-bit wide output, `Y`, representing the index of the highest bit set in `A`. The output `Valid` indicates whether a valid input was detected (specifically, whether at least one bit in `A` is high). If none of the bits are high, `Valid` is set to 0, and `Y` is assigned an undefined value.
module top_module(output reg [2:0] Y,
                 output reg Valid,
                 input wire [7:0] A
    );

code:
module top_module(output reg [2:0] Y,
                 output reg Valid,
                 input wire [7:0] A
    );always@(A)
begin
    Valid = 1;
    if (A[7]) Y = 7;
    else if (A[6]) Y = 6;
    else if (A[5]) Y = 5;
    else if (A[4]) Y = 4;
    else if (A[3]) Y = 3;
    else if (A[2]) Y = 2;
    else if (A[1]) Y = 1;
    else if (A[0]) Y = 0;
    else
        begin
                Valid = 0;
                Y = 3'bx;     
        end
  end    
endmodule

