description:
Design a frequency synthesizer that produces an output clock signal with a variable frequency based on the control word input. The circuit uses a reference clock (clk_ref) to increment a counter and a divider. The output clock (out_clk) toggles its state when the divider reaches a specified count (M), effectively dividing the reference frequency by a ratio set by parameters N and M. The synchronizing behavior of both the counter and divider ensures that the output clock frequency is stable and can be set by adjusting the control parameters.
module top_module(
  input clk_ref,
  input [31:0] ctrl_word,
  output reg out_clk
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_ref,
  input [31:0] ctrl_word,
  output reg out_clk
);parameter N = 10;
parameter M = 5;

reg [31:0] counter;
reg [31:0] divider;

always @(posedge clk_ref) begin
  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter == N-1) begin
    counter <= 0;
    divider <= divider + 1;
  end
end

always @(posedge clk_ref) begin
  if (divider == M-1) begin
    divider <= 0;
    out_clk <= ~out_clk;
  end
end

endmodule

