description:
Design a circuit that performs binary multiplication of two 8-bit unsigned integers, A and B. The module takes two 8-bit inputs and produces a 16-bit output representing the product. It utilizes a bitwise approach where each bit of the first input is examined, and if a bit is set, the corresponding shifted value of the second input is added to an accumulator. The output reflects the final accumulated sum, which is the result of the multiplication.
module top_module(
    input [7:0] A,
    input [7:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] Q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [7:0] A,
    input [7:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] Q
);reg [7:0] shift_reg;
reg [15:0] add_reg;
integer i;  // Declare i as an integer

always @ (A or B) begin
    shift_reg = B;
    add_reg = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
        if (A[i] == 1) begin
            add_reg = add_reg + (shift_reg << i);
        end
    end
    Q = add_reg;
end

endmodule

